| `install_sources.browser_download_host` | string or null | `null` | null, or an https URL with a host, a valid port if any, and no `@`, `?`, `#`, backslash, whitespace or control character | `scripts/install_sources.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `install_sources.browser_download_host` row; the Makefile's `fe-browsers` recipe | Set, `make fe-browsers` exports it as `PLAYWRIGHT_DOWNLOAD_HOST`, so the browser runner downloads its browser from that mirror; null exports nothing and leaves the caller's own `PLAYWRIGHT_DOWNLOAD_HOST`, or the runner's default host. A refused value stops the target with exit 14 before any download, never showing a value that holds an `@`. Absent, the reader writes `[using default] install_sources.browser_download_host = null` to stderr. | the system libraries `FE_BROWSER_FLAGS=--with-deps` installs, which come from the operating system's own package mirror | always |
